{"aligned_passages":[{"anchor":"gibbs-comparison","mapping_field":"claim_ids","mapping_ref":"sha256:1197ef489fa4b81b6170cd18c9ad07619ff01cff808caaa8df113602e3158c01/papers/long.json","paper_href":"/api/v1/papers/long?manifest=6c394d5e63870c0f51da2ffcc26ddf3c6c594d243a3282469fbc16661e9b3abf","passage_ref":"sha256:4c6350e9b4de8b6fa8cb1160f0ada57e4a2b797aebd0c518c88b1ace1b27878b/papers/long.md/sha256:1197ef489fa4b81b6170cd18c9ad07619ff01cff808caaa8df113602e3158c01/papers/long.json/passages/gibbs-comparison","query_href":"/api/v1/papers/query?manifest=6c394d5e63870c0f51da2ffcc26ddf3c6c594d243a3282469fbc16661e9b3abf&paper=long&passage=gibbs-comparison","reading_href":"/api/v1/papers/reading?manifest=6c394d5e63870c0f51da2ffcc26ddf3c6c594d243a3282469fbc16661e9b3abf&paper=long&passage=gibbs-comparison","span":{"end_byte":223137,"end_line":4910,"start_byte":221224,"start_line":4869},"stage":"long"}],"lenses":{"consumers":"/api/v1/graph?manifest=6c394d5e63870c0f51da2ffcc26ddf3c6c594d243a3282469fbc16661e9b3abf&view=arguments&node=scalar.finite_gibbs_comparison&direction=consumers&assumptions=true","direct_passages":"/api/v1/papers/query?manifest=6c394d5e63870c0f51da2ffcc26ddf3c6c594d243a3282469fbc16661e9b3abf&node=scalar.finite_gibbs_comparison&relation=direct","prerequisite_uses":"/api/v1/papers/query?manifest=6c394d5e63870c0f51da2ffcc26ddf3c6c594d243a3282469fbc16661e9b3abf&node=scalar.finite_gibbs_comparison&relation=prerequisites","prerequisites":"/api/v1/graph?manifest=6c394d5e63870c0f51da2ffcc26ddf3c6c594d243a3282469fbc16661e9b3abf&view=arguments&node=scalar.finite_gibbs_comparison&assumptions=true"},"neighborhood_href":"/api/v1/neighborhood?manifest=6c394d5e63870c0f51da2ffcc26ddf3c6c594d243a3282469fbc16661e9b3abf&ref=sha256%3Af22708f3180068944c06829213f78f6ecfb65ef34f6c8decded774b95a041d92%2Fnodes%2Fscalar.finite_gibbs_comparison","record":{"assumption_ids":[],"boundary":"Ordinary derivation in this authored edition, not an attribution of the whole synthesis to a cited external paper. The log-sum and entropy identities give the deterministic bounds; Gaussian concentration uses Lipschitz constant sqrt((n-1)/(2n^2)); counting configurations gives the conditional tail. Exact Gibbs sampling is a distributional premise, not an efficient sampling algorithm. The Born law and QAOA angle construction are distinct. No Lean or Comparator coverage and no complete formal dependency audit are asserted.","citation_ids":["authored_gibbs_comparison","scalar-r2-26-cite-parisi-formula"],"evidence_ids":["ordinary_comparison_warrants_20261024"],"id":"scalar.finite_gibbs_comparison","kind":"claim","label":"Finite Gibbs values and exact Gibbs samples","locator":"papers/qaoa-sk/long/reasoning-record.md §11.1.2, passage:gibbs-comparison; content-addressed source edition, not an external-paper attribution.","source_id":"authored_long_comparisons_20261024","statement":"For the pure zero-field SK Hamiltonian and beta>0, let L_n=max_sigma H_n(sigma)/n, F_n,beta=(n beta)^(-1)log sum_sigma exp(beta H_n(sigma)), and U_n,beta be the exact Gibbs mean energy per spin. For each instance, 0<=F_n,beta-L_n<=log(2)/beta and 0<=L_n-U_n,beta<=log(2)/beta. For n>=2 and s>0, P_J(|L_n-E L_n|>s)<=2 exp(-n^2 s^2/(n-1)). For an exact Gibbs draw Sigma, P(H_n(Sigma)/n<=L_n-s | J)<=min(1,exp(n(log(2)-beta s))). Since E L_n tends to P_*, both value expectations tend to P_* along every joint n→infinity,beta→infinity; an exact Gibbs draw tends to P_* in the joint disorder-and-sampling probability.","status":"unverified"},"ref":"sha256:f22708f3180068944c06829213f78f6ecfb65ef34f6c8decded774b95a041d92/nodes/scalar.finite_gibbs_comparison","relations":[{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:f22708f3180068944c06829213f78f6ecfb65ef34f6c8decded774b95a041d92/nodes/scalar.finite_gibbs_comparison","id":"sha256:f22708f3180068944c06829213f78f6ecfb65ef34f6c8decded774b95a041d92/edges/%5B%22scalar.finite_gibbs_comparison%22%2C%22scalar.parisi_formula%22%2C%22supports%22%5D","kind":"supports","record_ref":"sha256:f22708f3180068944c06829213f78f6ecfb65ef34f6c8decded774b95a041d92/edges/%5B%22scalar.finite_gibbs_comparison%22%2C%22scalar.parisi_formula%22%2C%22supports%22%5D","semantic_class":"curated_argument_support","to":"sha256:f22708f3180068944c06829213f78f6ecfb65ef34f6c8decded774b95a041d92/nodes/scalar.parisi_formula"},{"derived":true,"family":"provenance","from":"sha256:f22708f3180068944c06829213f78f6ecfb65ef34f6c8decded774b95a041d92/edges/%5B%22scalar.finite_gibbs_comparison%22%2C%22scalar.parisi_formula%22%2C%22supports%22%5D","id":"field:1307f55ed39bad9bec8e9068450cc8d25c808c80dcbd74e8c2e71907cfaeab73","kind":"from","owner_ref":"sha256:f22708f3180068944c06829213f78f6ecfb65ef34f6c8decded774b95a041d92/edges/%5B%22scalar.finite_gibbs_comparison%22%2C%22scalar.parisi_formula%22%2C%22supports%22%5D","semantic_class":"edge_endpoint_reference","source_field":"from","to":"sha256:f22708f3180068944c06829213f78f6ecfb65ef34f6c8decded774b95a041d92/nodes/scalar.finite_gibbs_comparison"},{"derived":true,"family":"provenance","from":"sha256:f22708f3180068944c06829213f78f6ecfb65ef34f6c8decded774b95a041d92/nodes/scalar.finite_gibbs_comparison","id":"field:14d44aaf11e178b0219668bd2506ac9c60c0457b034393c1773fd3ddb1204209","kind":"citation_ids","owner_ref":"sha256:f22708f3180068944c06829213f78f6ecfb65ef34f6c8decded774b95a041d92/nodes/scalar.finite_gibbs_comparison","semantic_class":"provenance_field_reference","source_field":"citation_ids","to":"sha256:f22708f3180068944c06829213f78f6ecfb65ef34f6c8decded774b95a041d92/citations/scalar-r2-26-cite-parisi-formula"},{"derived":true,"family":"provenance","from":"sha256:f22708f3180068944c06829213f78f6ecfb65ef34f6c8decded774b95a041d92/nodes/scalar.finite_gibbs_comparison","id":"field:6f7cd2cec15b1c479243507dfaa46af07c60909a9a1997d36182f1a1f95d606d","kind":"citation_ids","owner_ref":"sha256:f22708f3180068944c06829213f78f6ecfb65ef34f6c8decded774b95a041d92/nodes/scalar.finite_gibbs_comparison","semantic_class":"provenance_f